Mutations run against every check this change adds or touches, 2026-08-21.

A check nobody has watched fail is not a check. Each mutation below was applied
and the result recorded. Three of the mutation suites are permanent: they live
inside the scripts' own --self-check, which asserts the real files pass and then
that each named mutation fails, so `make test-scripts` re-runs all of them in
CI on every change.

scripts/test_caddy_console_auth_origin.py --self-check   15 mutations, all FAIL
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  the auth route deleted outright                                        FAIL
  the matcher definition deleted, leaving the handle pointing at nothing FAIL
  the prefix stripped before proxying                                    FAIL
  proxied to the internal listener instead of the public one             FAIL
  proxied straight to GoTrue, past every route refusal                   FAIL
  the Host rewrite dropped                                               FAIL
  the Host rewrite pinned to a literal that cannot follow the variable    FAIL
  the matcher widened until it takes the app's own sign-in page           FAIL
  the matcher narrowed to the bare form, dropping every real route        FAIL
  the app fallback hoisted above the auth route                           FAIL
  the app fallback no longer serving the app                              FAIL
  PostgREST published on the browser-facing origin                        FAIL
  caddy-console no longer handed the domain variable                      FAIL
  the two default domains drifted apart                                   FAIL
  the gateway's own public host expression changed without this following  FAIL

scripts/check-env-supabase-target.py --self-check   36 cases
-----------------------------------------------------------
Ten new must-fail cases, all FAIL:
  browser origin left on the hosted project after the auth origin moved
  only the bundle's origin moved
  the bundle's origin left unset
  the discovery origin left unset
  auth origin on a different host from the browser origin
  auth origin missing its /auth/v1 prefix
  site url left on loopback beside a public auth origin
  site url unset beside a public auth origin
  trailing slash on the site url
  (plus the pre-existing 21, re-based on the new fixture, still FAIL)

Two must-PASS cases, so the above cannot be satisfied by a check that simply
refuses any change to these values:
  the whole browser-facing origin moved together, coherently          PASS
  auth origin moved with SUPABASE_JWT_ISSUER left unset to inherit it PASS

One deliberate semantics change, called out rather than buried: the case
asserting that a browser-facing origin still naming the hosted project is
healthy is now a must-FAIL, and the assertion pins WHY it fails (the auth-origin
disagreement) and that it is NOT the server-side mixed-state rule, which still
ignores those two variables. A staged cutover that leaves the browser on the old
project while the issuer has already moved cannot log anyone in.

scripts/restore-storage-objects.py   parser and digest arms
-----------------------------------------------------------
--self-check, 9 cases, all as expected: a two-field manifest line, a five-field
line and a non-numeric size are each refused rather than skipped, since a
silently dropped line is an object nobody notices is missing.

Two live mutations against the running backend, both exercising an arm the
self-check cannot reach:
  a byte appended to one backup file      exit 1, "the backup file does not
                                          match its own manifest digest
                                          (4a1e3458767f vs 3c5d54ae5f1a),
                                          refusing to publish a corrupted
                                          object"
  the read-back URL pointed at a key
  that does not exist                     exit 1, "uploaded, but reading it
                                          back answered HTTP 400"
  storage.objects after both mutations    still exactly 15 rows, no strays

The second one matters most: without it, the read-back arm is untested and the
script would be trusting the upload's own 200, which is the exact thing it was
written not to do.

The check that could NOT be made to fail, and why that is a real gap
--------------------------------------------------------------------
The first version of test_caddy_console_auth_origin.py reported OK on a
Caddyfile that Caddy refuses to parse. `handle` takes exactly one matcher
token, so `handle /auth/v1 /auth/v1/*` is a parse error, and caddy-console
crash-looped on the box with "wrong argument count or unexpected line ending
after '/auth/v1/*'" while every structural check in this repo passed. Those
checks read the file as text; none of them can know what adapts.

Fixed twice over. The route is now a named matcher, which is the only form that
both parses and expresses a list, and the check reads it that way, so the
invalid form no longer satisfies it. And CI now runs `caddy validate` over all
five Caddyfiles with the same pinned image the services run, inside the
required repo-policy-lints job rather than a new non-required one. All five
adapt today.
